    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "For her project, Estefania transcribed interviews to document the impact of deportation on asylum seeking and migrant communities, as a result of third country asylum processing agreements. \"Life Facing Deportation\" was a one-year pilot inter-disciplinary research project co-designed by scholars in the UK, Guatemala, Mexico, the USA and Australia. It brought together scholars and practitioners from the fields of migration studies, law, health, education, ethics, development studies, anthropology, geography and sociology. The project adopted a rights-based and participatory approach to explore how asylum-seekers and returned migrants navigate and mitigate deficiencies in the asylum system and its inherent risks. \r\n\r\nStudent project deposited by department for archival purposes. Original work unavailable for public download due to permission restriction preferences of the author.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Ramirez, E. (2023). Life Facing Deportation. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/dm484bq7466. https://doi.org/10.25740/dm484bq7466.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
